WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:06.220
2019 has seen the loss of a myriad of hugely
talented actors with a range of different

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:10.140
backgrounds, from movies to television to
the Broadway stage.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.660
But while they may have made their names in
different worlds, they are all connected by

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:19.380
a true dedication to their craft, and by the
many fans who will miss them dearly.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:25.180
Three years after the death of R2-D2 actor
Kenny Baker, the man who brought Chewbacca

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:28.820
to life in the original Star Wars trilogy
also passed away.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:33.780
In a statement, the family of Peter Mayhew
confirmed that the towering actor died at

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.560
his Texas home on April 30th 2019.

00:00:37.129 --> 00:00:42.320
The statement celebrated Mayhew's life, focusing
on the experiences and lifelong friendships

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.359
that came from his time as part of the Star
Wars family.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:46.220
It read:

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:51.399
"As the films released and became more well-known
he had his eyes opened to the possibilities

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.440
of what he could achieve.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:57.880
For more than 30 years Peter traveled all
over the world spending time with his fans

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:58.900
and friends."

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.020
"Laugh it up, fuzzball."

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:07.440
But Mayhew did a lot more than just the convention
circuit.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:12.880
Over the years, he became heavily involved
with the 501st Legion, Wounded Warriors, Make-A-Wish,

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.380
and other non-profit organizations.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.320
In a tribute tweet, Mayhew's Star Wars co-star
Mark Hamill wrote:

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.400
"He was the gentlest of giants.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:26.390
A big man with an even bigger heart who never
failed to make me smile and a loyal friend

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:27.640
who I loved dearly.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:32.660
I'm grateful for the memories we shared and
I'm a better man for just having known him.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:33.480
Thanks Pete."

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:39.840
Against all odds, the previously wheelchair-bound
Mayhew returned to play Chewbacca in 2015's

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:44.200
The Force Awakens, his final on-screen appearance
as the iconic Wookiee.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:48.380
He is survived by his wife, Angie Mayhew,
and their three children.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:54.111
He may have been just 20 when he passed away
in his sleep following a seizure, but, according

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:58.420
to Disney, Cameron Boyce was, quote, "already
a veteran to show business."

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:03.440
The actor played the mischievous Luke Ross
in almost 100 episodes of the Disney series

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.640
Jessie, and later portrayed Carlos De Vil
in the Descendants franchise.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:14.200
Boyce also popped up in a number of more adult-oriented
projects, he was in K-horror remake Mirrors,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:19.100
and also appeared in the Adam Sandler comedy
Grown Ups as well as its 2012 sequel.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:24.519
Boyce's final project was Mrs. Fletcher, an
HBO comedy series that's due for release in

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:25.720
Fall 2019.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:30.080
On behalf of Boyce's family, a Disney Channel
spokesperson told CNN:

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:34.779
"From a young age, Cameron Boyce dreamed of
sharing his extraordinary artistic talents

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:35.560
with the world.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:41.079
He was an incredibly talented performer, a
remarkably caring and thoughtful person and,

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:46.240
above all else, he was a loving and dedicated
son, brother, grandson and friend.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:52.040
We offer our deepest condolences to his family,
castmates and colleagues and join his many

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:55.220
millions of fans in grieving his untimely
passing.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.000
He will be dearly missed."

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.960
Those who knew Boyce professionally took to
social media to share their shock and grief.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.440
Adam Sandler wrote:

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:04.280
"Too young.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.020
Too sweet.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:06.040
Too funny.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:09.880
Just the nicest, most talented, and most decent
kid around.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:10.960
Loved that kid."

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:18.160
Though he played founding MiB member Zed in
1997's Men in Black and dozens of other roles,

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:22.060
Rip Torn will always be remembered as Artie
from The Larry Sanders Show.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:26.080
After Torn's passing in July 2019, Variety
wrote:

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:30.359
"The Emmy-winning performance was perhaps
the best representation of Torn's unusual

00:03:30.359 --> 00:03:35.809
blend of toughness and tender sentimentality,
a turn that was as often profane as it was

00:03:35.809 --> 00:03:37.160
unexpectedly moving."

00:03:37.469 --> 00:03:42.220
Torn was nominated for an Emmy for every single
season in which he appeared on The Larry Sanders

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:47.540
Show, and he got another nod in 2008 after
a memorable guest appearance on 30 Rock, playing

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:50.260
Jack Donaghy's high-flying boss, Don Geiss.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.459
"Oh, hair like a Viking.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.280
God bless you."

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.900
His work on the big screen was lauded, too,
with the multi-talented Torn nominated for

00:03:57.919 --> 00:04:02.930
an Oscar in the Best Supporting Actor category
after portraying Mary Steenburgen's shotgun-happy

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.380
father in 1984's Cross Creek.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:10.480
According to his publicist, the Texas-born
actor passed away peacefully at his home in

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:10.980
Connecticut.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:12.240
He was 88.

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:17.880
Best-known to international audiences for
his engrossing performance as Blade Runner

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:23.540
antagonist Roy Batty, Rutger Hauer passed
away in July 2019 after a short illness.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.040
He was 75.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:30.300
Blade Runner was Hauer's second American movie,
though he was already a veteran in the Netherlands

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.300
by that point.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:35.370
The towering Dutchman entered the industry
after serving in the military, striking up

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:39.190
a fruitful working relationship with his fellow
Dutchman, Paul Verhoeven.

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:44.010
The auteur cast him in the eponymous role
for his TV series Floris, and they would later

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:49.650
work together on period drama Katie Tippel,
WWII epic Soldier of Orange, and art-house

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:50.960
drama Spetters.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:55.900
And while 1982's Blade Runner was a critical
flop upon release, the movie soon went on

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.380
to become a cult classic.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:02.380
Hauer's "tears in rain" monologue, which he
wrote himself, is now considered an iconic

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:07.180
moment in the history of cinema, and a perfect
example of his "gentle giant" nature.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:14.200
"All those moments will be lost in time."

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:18.840
After Hauer's passing, Blade Runner director
Ridley Scott said:

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:22.900
"I don't know who was more nervous on that
first morning of the first day on set.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.680
We helped each other through the entire process
because it was very challenging.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:27.700
I'll miss him."

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:32.780
Hauer became a prolific character actor in
the years that followed, popping up in Sin

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:36.780
City, Batman Begins, True Blood and countless
genre films.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:40.540
He is survived by his wife of 50 years and
his daughter.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:45.680
Actress and former model Peggy Lipton, who
first made a name for herself in the late

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:50.900
'60s playing hippie cop Julie Barnes on The
Mod Squad, passed away from cancer in May

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:51.720
2019.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:56.500
In a statement, Lipton's daughters, Parks
and Recreation actress Rashida Jones and her

00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:02.160
sister Kidada, said that their mother passed
away surrounded by family at the age of 72.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.320
The statement read:

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:07.260
"She made her journey peacefully with her
daughters and nieces by her side.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:10.320
We feel so lucky for every moment we spent
with her.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:15.220
We can't put all of our feelings into words
right now but we will say: Peggy was, and

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:19.000
will always be our beacon of light, both in
this world and beyond."

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:23.580
Despite winning a Golden Globe for her work
on The Mod Squad, Lipton once took a long

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:26.340
break from acting, sitting out most of the
'80s.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:32.000
She appeared back on the scene in 1990, however,
when she appeared as Norma Jennings in David

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.900
Lynch's surreal TV series Twin Peaks.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:39.720
Speaking to the Georgian Journal in 2017,
the year she reprised the role on the show's

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:43.680
critically-acclaimed comeback, Lipton recalled
her first meeting with Lynch.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:44.300
She said:

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:50.280
"I arrived and he and Mark Frost, his co-writer
and producer, sat at a large table with nothing

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:51.520
on it but my photo.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:55.220
I shot the pilot and the feeling inside me
was pure excitement.

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:56.840
I loved being Norma."

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:03.460
Maine-born actress Stephanie Niznik passed
away unexpectedly in California on June 23rd,

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.600
2019, at the age of 52.

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:10.360
Niznik majored in Russian and theater and
would go on to hone her acting skills at the

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.380
California Institute of the Arts.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:17.240
After graduating from Cal Arts she landed
a part in the Dan Aykroyd led comedy Exit

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.260
to Eden, her feature film debut.

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:24.240
Niznik became a TV regular in the years that
followed, and is perhaps best-known for her

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:29.220
time on the WB show Everwood, in which she
portrayed caring next door neighbor Nina Feeney.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:33.380
In a joint statement after her passing, Everwood's
creators said:

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:38.190
"She continued that role off-screen by being
an incredible friend, a nurturing mother figure

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:43.350
to our younger cast members and an artist
who brought warmth, compassion and humor to

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:45.100
every episode and our set.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:49.020
Everyone who was lucky enough to know and
work with her will miss her dearly."

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:55.100
Niznik was also well-known to Star Trek fans;
she played Trill Starfleet Ensign Kell Perim

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:58.300
in 1998 feature film Star Trek: Insurrection.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:03.620
She also later popped up in the Star Trek:
Enterprise TV series, appearing as a humanoid

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:06.620
Wraith in the season one episode "Rogue Planet".

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:13.660
Famed New York socialite and two-time Oscar
nominee Sylvia Miles passed away in June 2019.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:15.200
She was 94.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:20.680
Speaking to Page Six, actress Geraldine Smith
revealed that Miles had recently moved out

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:21.540
of a care home.

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:24.300
Smith, a longtime friend of Miles, said:

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.660
"She didn't want to die there.

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:28.820
We went out for a big lunch to celebrate her
coming home.

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:32.190
She was very excited and telling us to order
whatever we wanted.

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:34.300
'Order drinks; order desserts!'

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:35.800
We had a wonderful time."

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:40.500
Miles was well-known for being the life of
the party and was frequently spotted at swanky

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:43.600
social events with fellow New York resident
Andy Warhol.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:48.900
Speaking to People in 1976, Miles revealed
that she was always on the guest list for

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:51.920
the top shindigs, because she knew how to
have a good time.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:52.720
She explained:

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:54.460
"I get invited because I'm fun.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:56.050
I have a good sense of humor.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:56.840
I look good.

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:58.580
I'm not bad to have at a party."

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:04.540
One of her most notable films, 1972's Heat,
was produced by Warhol, but Miles will no

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:11.620
doubt be best remembered for her sassy turns
in 1969's Midnight Cowboy and 1975's Farewell,

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:12.240
My Lovely.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:17.651
Amazingly, she was nominated in the Best Supporting
Actress category for both movies, despite

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:21.040
only being onscreen for a combined total of
11 minutes.

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:27.960
Manhattan-born railroad heiress Gloria Vanderbilt
passed away at her New York home in June 2019,

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:31.520
having recently been diagnosed with an advanced
form of stomach cancer.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:32.800
She was 95.

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:38.160
Vanderbilt began her acting career in 1957,
but she was already well-known by the time

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:39.280
she made her debut.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:43.820
She was just 10 years old when she became
the subject of a high-profile court battle

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:48.110
between her widowed mother, Gloria Morgan
Vanderbilt, and her paternal aunt, Gertrude

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:53.080
Vanderbilt Whitney, both of whom sought custody
of her and control over her trust fund.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:57.700
After that, Vanderbilt set out to prove she
was more than the "poor little rich girl"

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.460
portrayed by the newspaper headlines.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:05.100
She landed roles on several Golden Era anthology
shows during the late '50s and early '60s,

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:07.560
quickly establishing herself as an actress.

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:12.880
She also appeared in Adventures in Paradise,
an exotic ABC show about a Korean War vet

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:18.290
living in the Pacific, and The Love Boat,
a cruise ship-set comedy that ran from 1977

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:19.380
to 1987.

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:24.240
She was known for much more than her acting,
however, becoming particularly known as a

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:25.330
fashion designer.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:30.160
Her son, Anderson Cooper, was keen to highlight
this in his statement after her passing.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:30.900
He said:

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:36.200
"Gloria Vanderbilt was an extraordinary woman,
who loved life, and lived it on her own terms.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:42.120
She was a painter, a writer, and designer
but also a remarkable mother, wife, and friend."

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:48.900
Canadian actress Stefanie Sherk, wife of Oscar-nominee
Demian Bichir, passed away "peacefully" in

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:50.000
April 2019.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:54.920
The actor confirmed his wife's death in a
heartbreaking Instagram post, calling it "the

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.860
saddest and toughest time" of his life.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:57.700
He wrote:

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:01.120
"We don't know how much time it will take
for us to overcome this pain.

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:06.280
Stefanie's beautiful, angelical and talented
presence will be immensely missed."

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:09.580
The cause of death was soon confirmed as suicide.

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:14.920
After the Los Angeles County Medical Examiner-Coroner
made the information public, Bichir went into

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:18.720
more detail about the "invisible affliction"
that Sherk had been dealing with.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:22.460
In a second Instagram post that has since
been deleted, he wrote:

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:27.000
"It was our hope that we would have some time
to heal and grieve before we could talk about

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:30.140
this issue that affects way too many people
around the globe.

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:35.280
Depression has taken the lives of so many
beautiful, wonderful, talented people such

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:37.300
as my beloved wife, Stefanie."

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:41.680
Sadly, these aren't the only actors who have
left us in 2019.

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:46.620
Here are some of the other stars who enhanced
our lives before leaving us all too soon.

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:48.160
Russi Taylor

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:52.000
Carmine Caridi

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.320
Geneviève Waïte

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:00.300
Barbara Perry

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:06.960
If you or anyone you know is having suicidal
thoughts, please call the National Suicide

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:11.730
Prevention Lifeline at 1-800-273-TALK (8255).

